






@(1 = 1-2) Say to my lord: this is what @wPN{Aradŋu}, your servant, says:

@(3 = 3-8) You instructed me, as I was taking the direct route to @wGN{Subir}, to secure your provincial taxes, to inform myself precisely as to the state of the territory, and to ensure its obedience by taking counsel with (?) @wPN{Apillaša}, the 'Sage of the Assembly', so that he could thus return the people of @wGN{Subir} to their customary way of speaking (?).

@(9 = 9-11) But when I arrived at the palace gate, no one enquired after the well-being of my lord. No one rose from their seat before me, or bowed down.  @vart[t3101.v1,t3101.v1]{@varn{1 ms. adds:} They intimidated me. }

@(12 = 12-18)  @varh[t3101.v2]{When I came nearer } @vart[t3101.v3,t3101.v2]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} …… carries …… } -- well, your wayside hostel where carding-combs (?) and lances inlaid with gold, silver, cornelian and lapis lazuli have been set up, covers an area of one hectare! @wPN{Apillaša} himself is decked out in  @varh[t3101.v4]{gold and lapis lazuli } @vart[t3101.v5,t3101.v4]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} lapis lazuli, gold, silver and cornelian }, and he sits on a raised throne furnished with a rich raiment. His feet rest upon a golden footstool. He would not remove his feet in my presence!

